SUMMARY:Zeta Values as Moments: A Random Matrix Theory
DESCRIPTION:The values of the Riemann zeta-function $\\zeta\\left(\\alpha+\
 \beta n\\right)$ with $\\alpha>1$\, $\\beta>0$ and $n$ a positive integer 
 can be viewed as moments of a probability distribution. In my talk I will 
 construct the corresponding random matrix model and determine its asymptot
 ic spectral curve\, which exhibits an unusual feature\, the complete asymp
 totics of its partition function and uniform approx\nhttps://indico.math.c
 nrs.fr/event/17408/
LOCATION:IHES
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17408/
