SUMMARY:Origami Tori
DESCRIPTION:An origami torus is a piecewise affine isometric embedding of a
  flat torus into R 3 . It is surprising that these things exist\, but than
 ks to the work of Burago and Zalgaller in 1960 they do. 30 years later\, B
 &Z proved that every flat torus is realized as an origami torus. In 2023\,
  Lazarus and Tallerie proved that you can realize all flat tori using a si
 ngle underlying triangulation with about 250\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/
 event/17062/
LOCATION:IHES
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17062/
